  "comments": [
    {
      "path": "ForServer/tests/transport_tests.cpp",
      "content": "This test also passes if cancellation is completely ignored: with no listener on 127.0.0.1:1, the connection failure satisfies EXPECT_THROW(std::exception). It therefore does not establish that a canceled download never sends a request. Use a controlled local listener/mock and assert that no request is received, or assert a cancellation-specific error distinct from connection failures.",
      "existing_code": "    EXPECT_THROW(request_http(endpoint, \"/frame\", \"NGSREQ3 1 m-test 8 8 0 0 1 rgba 0\"),\n                 std::exception);",
      "start_line": 59,
      "end_line": 60,
      "category": "test",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "ForServer/tools/cloud_benchmark.py",
      "content": "Writing the captured packet now occurs inside the measured interval, so `elapsed_seconds` and `frames_per_second` include local disk I/O rather than just HTTP throughput. This can materially skew short runs (including the supported `--frames 1`) or runs on slow storage. Retain the first payload while collecting samples, stop the timer, and then write `frame.ngsf`, as the previous timing boundary did.",
      "existing_code": "            if payload is not None:\n                (output / \"frame.ngsf\").write_bytes(payload)",
      "start_line": 59,
      "end_line": 60,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "ForServer/deploy/deploy.sh",
      "content": "Select architectures from the effective configuration when preserving an existing installation. `configure` leaves config.json unchanged unless `--reconfigure` is supplied, but this query uses the command-line devices (default `0`). For example, an installation configured for an SM75 GPU at index 1 upgraded without `--devices` on a machine with an SM89 GPU at index 0 now builds only SM89 code/PTX, which cannot execute on the configured SM75 GPU. Previously querying all GPUs covered that case. Read the preserved configuration's devices before querying, or continue compiling for all installed GPUs.",
      "existing_code": "capabilities=$(nvidia-smi -i \"$devices\" --query-gpu=compute_cap --format=csv,noheader | tr -d '.' | sort -u)",
      "start_line": 107,
      "end_line": 107,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high"
    },
    {
      "path": "ForServer/src/windows_http.cpp",
      "content": "This closes an active synchronous WinHTTP handle from another thread. request_http opens its session with flags=0 and performs synchronous SendRequest/ReceiveResponse/ReadData calls, while the UI calls cancel() during navigation or shutdown. WinHTTP does not support closing a handle while a synchronous call on it is in progress; the mutex only serializes attach/release and does not protect those calls. Internet also retains the closed handle for subsequent operations. Use an asynchronous WinHTTP request with cancellation-safe completion/lifetime handling, or defer closure until the synchronous worker has finished (with bounded waits and cancellation checks). Add a regression test that cancels while a server stalls response headers or body; the existing pre-canceled test does not exercise this race.",
      "existing_code": "    if (impl_-\u003ehandle)\n        WinHttpCloseHandle(std::exchange(impl_-\u003ehandle, nullptr));",
      "start_line": 32,
      "end_line": 33,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high"
    },
    {
      "path": "ForServer/deploy/deploy.sh",
      "content": "Stop any supervisor started by this upgrade before restoring the files and symlinks. If startup is interrupted (e.g. Ctrl-C while `service.py start` is polling health), its detached `run` process survives: `start` only calls `stop_service` on its normal timeout path. This EXIT handler then restores the old configuration/current release while the new gateway remains running, leaving a mixed installation and preventing a clean retry. Track whether this transaction attempted startup and shut down its owned supervisor using the new configuration/supervisor before rollback.",
      "existing_code": "    if [[ \"$result\" != 0 ]]; then\n        for name in config.json service.py; do",
      "start_line": 134,
      "end_line": 135,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "high"
    }
  ],
